    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "A positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > and a permutation of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22480136d759f23bb7990708cbe1bb46c6939997.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,a_3,\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" > is given such that for all indices <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/a/b5a34e30e58c809ae4190130823ed7524fdd3dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i\\geq 10^{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" >,</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec3ea9538d92a4c782dffb912b1d8f1546532c63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_{i+1}-a_{i}|\\leq 2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" > holds. Prove that there exists infinity many indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"8\" height=\"16\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606c17ee63368909e5b4cc2eec01fe58c3d8293f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_j -j|&lt; d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "A positive integer $d$ and a permutation of positive integers $a_1,a_2,a_3,\\dots$ is given such that for all indices $i\\geq 10^{100}$, $|a_{i+1}-a_{i}|\\leq 2d$ holds. Prove that there exists infinity many indices $j$ such that $|a_j -j|< d$.",
