    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 1671272,
    "poster_id": 209049,
    "post_rendered": "Let <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe57e92ad73151b514cb7359dd033da38c02040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\ldots a_n,k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" >,</span> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > be positive integers such that<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c098208177e6dbfa7777efef4c94ae257ca8625e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{a_n}=k\\quad\\text{and}\\quad a_1a_2\\cdots a_n=M.$$\"  width=\"371\" height=\"39\" >If <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee948e5be4abc2202e7bbb31e25748f0add452e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" >,</span> prove that the polynomial<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e723cdce4a9b586e273f8b4228309f3bb3c12016.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$P(x)=M(x+1)^k-(x+a_1)(x+a_2)\\cdots (x+a_n)$$\"  width=\"387\" height=\"20\" >has no positive roots.",
    "post_canonical": "Let $a_1,a_2,\\ldots a_n,k$, and $M$ be positive integers such that\n$$\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{a_n}=k\\quad\\text{and}\\quad a_1a_2\\cdots a_n=M.$$\nIf $M>1$, prove that the polynomial\n$$P(x)=M(x+1)^k-(x+a_1)(x+a_2)\\cdots (x+a_n)$$\nhas no positive roots.",
    "username": "math90",
